Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The decoder and encoder are original implementations written from ITU-T
Recommendation T.81 | ISO/IEC 10918-1 (freely published by the ITU), ITU-T
T.871 (JFIF), the EXIF specification (CIPA DC-008), the ICC specification
(ICC.1, the embedding of profiles in JPEG) and Adobe's description of its
APP14 colour-transform segment. They are not translations of, and do not
derive from, any other JPEG implementation's source. The tables of T.81
Annex K (quantisation and Huffman examples) and Table D.3 (the arithmetic
coder's probability estimation) are reproduced from the Recommendation;
docs/PROVENANCE.md records how.

libjpeg-turbo was used only as a black box (a binary library, through the
imagecodecs and Pillow Python packages, offline): to make some of the test
files in tests/corpus/gen and to render references for them, and to decode
this encoder's output for comparison. None of its code is included or was
consulted.

